{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778079218,"nonce":"VwMoUP7aJkNntOhMso0FVj6V6jc=","message":"Reproduced again today (2026-05-06):\n\n- Auth request 6ce9e43e for feature/synthesis-review failed at execution: working tree was dirty with untracked results/part2_5/runpod/... files, exit_code=1.\n- API and inbox both reported status='completed', exit_code=1.\n- The UserPromptSubmit hook (mandible-inbox-check.sh) surfaces only .status, never .exit_code. The resulting system-reminder read: '[mandible-inbox] auth_result 6ce9e43e — branch: feature/synthesis-review — status: completed'. The orchestrating agent interpreted 'completed' as 'succeeded' and reported the merge as gone through.\n\nHook-side framing (in addition to the API-side framing already in this issue):\n\nThe hook is the most direct consumer of the ambiguity. Even after the API is fixed, the hook string format should be unambiguous on its own. A one-line jq change in mandible-inbox-check.sh (compute outcome from exit_code at format time) closes today's symptom without a daemon rebuild.\n\nCode-level state today:\n\n- DB has separate `status` (lifecycle) and `exit_code` columns.\n- auth-queue.ts:884 (storeExecutionResult) writes status='completed' unconditionally regardless of exit code.\n- isFailedLike() at auth-queue.ts:1047 already correctly checks exit_code != 0, but is only used for internal queue logic — never surfaced to consumers.\n- Hook at .config/scripts/mandible-inbox-check.sh:25 formats only .status.\n\nProposed fix (small, two-step, non-breaking):\n\n1. Hook-side, immediate: in mandible-inbox-check.sh, change the jq format to derive an outcome ('succeeded' | 'failed (exit_code=N)' | 'rejected' | etc.). Pure shell change, no daemon rebuild.\n2. API-side, durable: add a derived `outcome` field to buildResolvedPayload() (auth-queue.ts:1036) using the existing isFailedLike() logic. `outcome` joins `status`, doesn't replace it. Future consumers (dashboard, pollers) get the unambiguous signal.\n\nRenaming `status` → `lifecycle` (rejected option) is too invasive for the actual benefit.\n\nFiled 13f7c92 today before searching prior art — closing it as duplicate of this issue.\n\nBranches in progress: hook-side fix (dotfiles), API-side fix (mandible).","files":null}]}